{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310619,"nonce":"RQXcuood+Uf1yX9sNyhWIErP5+0=","title":"`var f = static_fn; f();` SIGSEGV'd — Variable handler used build_function_ptr (raw fn_addr) but CallIndirect expects {fn_ptr, env_ptr} ...","message":"`var f = worker; f();` SIGSEGV'd at the indirect call. Root cause: representation mismatch between function-as-value lowering and indirect-call dispatch.\n\n**Cranelift's CallIndirect** ([compiler/src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs:2826](compiler/src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs#L2826)) unifies its dispatch on closure objects — it assumes the func_ptr register holds a pointer to `{fn_ptr: i64, env_ptr: i64}`:\n\n```\nbuilder.ins().load(types::I64, MemFlags::new(), closure_ptr, 0)  // fn_ptr\nbuilder.ins().load(types::I64, MemFlags::new(), closure_ptr, 8)  // env_ptr\n```\n\nThe Variable handler for `SymbolKind::Function` at [hir_to_mir.rs:7945](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L7945) used `build_function_ptr` which emits `IrValue::Function(func_id)` → Cranelift's `func_addr(I64, func_ref)` → raw machine address of the function. The two loads then read the first 16 bytes of the function's executable code as `{fn_ptr, env_ptr}` and the indirect call jumped to that garbage → SIGSEGV.\n\nFixed in `4882aee` by switching to `build_function_ref(func_id)`. The `FunctionRef` IR op is already lowered to allocate a 16-byte closure object with `fn_ptr = func_addr(...)` and `env_ptr = NULL`. This is the unified representation CallIndirect expects.\n\n**Bound method refs** (`var d = obj.describe`) go through `MakeClosure`, which produces the same `{fn_ptr, env_ptr}` shape, so they were never affected. The bug was specifically the bare static/free function reference path.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- If a new lowering path produces a function value that may be CallIndirect'd, it MUST use `FunctionRef` or `MakeClosure`, never raw `IrValue::Function`. The raw form is only safe for direct calls (CallDirect with a known func_id).\n- Reflect.callMethod's call site at [hir_to_mir.rs:7263](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L7263) already does the right thing — keep that pattern.\n\n**Cache caveat for regression test runs:** `run_haxe_tests.sh` only clears `.rayzor/blade/cache/*.blade`, not `.rayzor/cache/*.mir.cache`. After a fix to the MIR lowering, you must also `rm -rf .rayzor/cache/` (or remove the whole `.rayzor/` dir) to invalidate stale MIR caches; otherwise tests that should pass after the fix will still show the pre-fix crash because the cached MIR is unchanged. This is how `test_thread_spawn_function_value` showed as still failing in my first regression run after the fix.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_function_ref_indirect_call` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}